{"item_id": "feed:https://www.treelinereview.com/gearreviews/rei-co-op-magma-30-sleeping-bag-review", "version_id": "4c742dc416136bc209dcfd4b570e69002f847ac2b7c81e9b48b874b0de19bfd8", "decision": "accept", "reason": "Sleeping bags are in scope under weather and survival gear (sleep systems), and the review's multi-season, multi-location field testing (Idaho, Montana, California; 33°F lows, rain, damp redwood camping) speaks to Mammoth-relevant conditions like weight carried and performance in damp weather. Under Credibility, the tester's measured weight and temperature observations are first-hand, though the review is from an affiliate-model publisher, which the Commercial incentives section requires us to note; the tester also reports former outdoor educator background, not Mammoth participation. The 2026 publication notes both praise and drawbacks (bulk in smaller packs, insulated yoke), satisfying Diversity of perspectives, and the review is a single independent source, so claims are attributed to it. Best supports Piece 02 (manufacturer warmth and weight claims versus field testing) and Piece 03 (practical tradeoffs for packing and weight).", "piece_ids": ["02", "03"]}
{"item_id": "feed:https://www.treelinereview.com/gearreviews/best-running-pants", "version_id": "28be243117027254a6e4779fa7e5a25dbdf399fec0a6fbae1b105b46113f8b20", "decision": "defer", "reason": "Running pants fall within clothing and protection, but this roundup is a multi-product review driven by a single tester's subjective ratings and a one-off sink water test, and it relies on an affiliate model with no Mammoth-specific context, so under Credibility and Commercial incentives its evidence is too thin to rely on yet. Mammoth-relevant conditions (rucking, weight carried for days, durability under load) are not tested, and the central argument rests on one tester in the Northeast rather than the three independent publishers the Uncertainty section requires. Deferred items may be reconsidered if stronger evidence appears.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://www.treelinereview.com/gearreviews/best-down-vests", "version_id": "22e47cddced54dfcbfaf1a331606c33343356dcc4b8c256dce2a2ea8ed1ab743", "decision": "defer", "reason": "Insulated vests are clothing and protection and would be in scope, but this roundup of women's vests offers mainly subjective, single-tester observations with an affiliate model, and several entries (Arc'teryx Atom, Arc'teryx Cerium, Mountain Hardwear Ghost Whisperer) are explicitly untested by the publisher. Under Credibility, the Uncertainty section's three-publisher requirement is unmet, and the piece does not address Mammoth conditions such as carrying weight over multiple days, so the evidence is insufficient to rely on yet. Deferred items may be reconsidered if stronger evidence appears.", "piece_ids": []}
